<article class="env-lemma" id="0DFZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DFZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0DFZ">84.4.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a henselian local ring. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $A$ such that $f : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is a proper morphism. Let $X_0 \subset X$ be the fibre of $f$ over the closed point. For any sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ we have $\Gamma (X, \mathcal{F}) = \Gamma (X_0, \mathcal{F}|_{X_0})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DFY" data-tag="0DFY">84.4.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>